<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
      The app's own theme colours (2026-10-12). Until now styles.xml named
      @color/colorPrimary and @color/colorPrimaryDark and the app defined
      neither, so Capacitor's defaults applied (#3F51B5 indigo, #303F9F).

      Both are the icon family's navy #00286D, the mark's own darkest colour:
      it is the one icon colour that holds white system text and icons
      (13.78:1; the teal end, #00BB9F, gives 2.44:1), and it is the colour the
      launcher icon starts from, so the system's tint for the app and the icon
      agree.

      colorAccent is deliberately NOT defined here. It tints controls inside
      the app (selection handles, native widgets), which makes it a screen
      colour, and screen colours belong to the design-system step. It still
      falls back to Capacitor's #FF4081; see WORK-QUEUE.md.
    -->
    <color name="colorPrimary">#00286D</color>
    <color name="colorPrimaryDark">#00286D</color>
</resources>
